## Why This Is Asked
Assess ability to design governance-aware, low-latency LLM gating in multi-tenant contexts with compliance, verifiable provenance, and drift detection.

## Key Concepts
- Policy schema design for strict data governance
- Real-time evaluation and routing with canary semantics
- Tamper-evident logging and prompt hashing
- Drift and latency testing in distributed infra

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple policy eval skeleton
function evaluatePolicy(prompt, policy) {
  const redacted = applyRedaction(prompt, policy.redaction_rules);
  const hash = hashPrompt(redacted, policy);
  const allowed = policy.allowed;
  return { allowed, redacted, hash };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test drift across regions?
- How would you ensure logs remain tamper-evident during partial outages?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design adaptive residency and tenancy policy in a real multi-tenant LLM gateway, handling regulatory events, drift alerts, and auditable changes.

## Key Concepts
- Policy as code with per-tenant residency and retention rules
- Dynamic tenancy routing and hot-updatable policies
- Drift detection, versioning, rollback, and tamper-evident auditing
- API design, data models, and test coverage

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal policy model (JS-like)
function TenantPolicy(tenantId, residency, retentionDays, piiHandling, version, lastUpdated) {
  this.tenantId = tenantId;
  this.residency = residency; // 'on-prem'|'private-cloud'|'shared'
  this.retentionDays = retentionDays;
  this.piiHandling = piiHandling; // 'redact'|'anonymize'|'allow'
  this.version = version;
  this.lastUpdated = lastUpdated;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you implement drift detection and rollback strategy?
- What metrics and tests validate residency switches without SLA breach?

## Why This Is Asked
Real-world needs balance cost, latency, and reliability across tenants. This asks for a concrete policy language, a routing strategy, and test plans under varying traffic. It also probes drift handling and failover.

## Key Concepts
- Per-tenant QoS policies
- Multi-model routing with cost/latency prediction
- Data locality and failover strategies
- Observability: audit logs, drift tests

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo routing sketch
function route(req, tenant) {
  const p = policy[tenant];
  const candidates = models.filter(m => p.preferredModels.includes(m.name));
  // pick cheapest that meets latency
  return candidates
    .map(m => ({m, est: predict(m, req)}))
    .filter(x => x.est.lat <= p.max_latency)
    .sort((a,b) => a.est.cost - b.est.cost)[0]?.m;
}
```

